{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He appeared to him.</b> To visit the sick. Rabbi Chama bar Chanina said: it was the third day from his circumcision, and the Holy One, blessed be He, came and inquired after his welfare (Bava Metzia 86)." "<b>In the plains of Mamre.</b> He it was who gave him counsel concerning the circumcision; therefore He appeared to him in his portion (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Sitting.</b> ישב is written. He sought to stand, but the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: Sit, and I will stand — and you are a sign for your children that I am destined to stand in the assembly of judges while they sit, as it says: ״אֱלֹהִים נִצָּב בַּעֲדַת אֵל״ (Psalms 82) (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>The tent entrance.</b> To see if any passerby was about, so he could bring them into his house." "<b>Like the heat of the day.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, took the sun out of its sheath, so as not to trouble him with guests; and because He saw him distressed that no guests were coming, He brought the angels upon him in the likeness of men (Bava Metzia ibid.)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:09.601493820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}